Remove the conditional @phpstan-this-out annotation from Collection::prepend().

illuminate/collections v13.33.0 uses a PHPStan-only conditional type based on a
method parameter ("$key is null ? ..."), which Psalm (6.x and 7.x) cannot parse:
conditional types are only allowed on templates. Psalm crashes with
"Unrecognized template '$key'" while scanning vendor autoload files.

The annotation only affects static-analysis precision of vendor code, so
removing it is safe.

--- a/Collection.php
+++ b/Collection.php
@@ -1058,8 +1058,6 @@
      * @param  TValue  $value
      * @param  TKey|null  $key
      * @return $this
-     *
-     * @phpstan-this-out ($key is null ? static<TKey|int, TValue> : $this)
      */
     public function prepend($value, $key = null)
     {
